            <ArticleTitle>Discovery of P2X3 selective antagonists for the treatment of chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2565-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2012.01.124</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Purinergic receptor P2X3 has been linked to analgesia in a number of pre-clinical models of pain, and is expressed in the human pain perception pathway. Only few P2X3-selective antagonists have been reported to date. This Letter describes the SAR and in vivo analgesic profile of a novel scaffold of selective P2X3 antagonists.</AbstractText>
